# What the shared em and en dash gate (@cosyte/script-utils, `cosyte-no-emdash`) leaves out here.
# It reads every other tracked file, and every tracked file's name. One entry per line, anchored at
# the repository root; an entry that matches no tracked path is refused.

# THE CHANGELOG'S ARCHIVE, and only the archive. Every entry above "Released before this file was
# generated" is written by the release from a changeset and is read for both dashes like any other
# file. From that heading down is the frozen archive of releases before the changelog generator,
# which is never hand-edited. It holds an en dash and, in an entry describing an earlier dash gate,
# an encoded em dash, so the archive is not read at all rather than read for the em dash alone. A
# heading the file no longer carries is refused, so this cannot outlive its subject.
CHANGELOG.md unread below ## Released before this file was generated
